@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Bookmark a show, listing, or search - Lively Help Center";
    ViewData["CategorySlug"] = "Buying";
    ViewData["SubCategorySlug"] = "Buying items";
    ViewData["HeroTitle"] = "Bookmark a show, listing, or search";
    ViewData["HeroStyle"] = "background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(0,0,0,0.4), rgba(0,0,0,0.4)), url('/help_centre_img/help_area/help_centre_hero_bg.png');";
    ViewData["IsArticle"] = true;
}

<div class="article-detail-page">
    <div class="article-body">

        <div>
            Bookmarking lets you save upcoming shows, specific listings, and product searches you're interested in so you can find them later and get notified about them.
        </div>

        <div class="article-info-box">
            <strong>Tip:</strong> If you want to be notified anytime a seller goes live (not just for a single show or product), you can <strong>Follow</strong> the seller from their profile.
        </div>

        <p class="mt-4"><strong>In this article:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="#how-bookmarks-work">How bookmarks work</a></li>
            <li><a href="#bookmark-show-or-product">Bookmark a show or</a> product</li>
            <li><a href="#bookmark-a-search">Bookmark a search</a></li>
            <li><a href="#view-your-bookmarks">View your bookmarks</a></li>
            <li><a href="#remove-a-bookmark">Remove a bookmark</a></li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="how-bookmarks-work">How bookmarks work</h2>
        <p>When you bookmark something:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>It's added to your Saved list under the Activity tab</li>
            <li>You'll get a notification when a bookmarked show or product goes live, or new results match a saved search (make sure <a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">notifications are enabled</a>)</li>
            <li>Bookmarking is anonymous, so sellers and other buyers can only see the total number of bookmarks, not who saved them</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="text-center my-4">
            <img src="/help_centre_img/help_area/how_bookmarks_work.png"
                 alt="Bookmark saved list and search results in Lively app"
                 class="img-fluid"
                 style="border-radius: 12px;" />
        </div>

        <h2 id="bookmark-show-or-product">Bookmark a show or product</h2>
        <ol>
            <li>Open the show or product listing you want to save.</li>
            <li>Tap or click the <strong>bookmark</strong> icon to save it.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2 id="bookmark-a-search">Bookmark a search</h2>
        <p>Save a product search to be notified when new matching products are listed.</p>
        <ol>
            <li>Run your product search (for example, by keyword, category, or brand).</li>
            <li>On the search results page, tap or click <strong>Save this Search.</strong></li>
            <li><strong>Confirm</strong> that you want to receive notifications</li>
        </ol>
        <p><strong>Note:</strong> You can't save searches for Shows, Categories, or Users.</p>

        <h2 id="view-your-bookmarks">View your bookmarks</h2>
        <p>You'll see all your saved shows, products, and searches in one place.</p>
        <ol>
            <li>From Lively's home screen, open your <strong>Activity</strong> tab.</li>
            <li>Select <strong>Saved</strong> to view your list.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2 id="remove-a-bookmark">Remove a bookmark</h2>
        <p>When you remove a bookmark, it'll disappear from your Saved list, and you'll no longer receive notifications about it.</p>
        <ol>
            <li>From Lively's home screen, open your <strong>Activity</strong> tab.</li>
            <li>Select <strong>Saved.</strong></li>
            <li>
                Remove the bookmark:
                <ul>
                    <li>For saved shows or products: Tap the <strong>bookmark icon</strong> again. When the icon changes from solid to empty, the bookmark is removed.</li>
                    <li>For saved searches: Tap the <strong>menu icon</strong> on the left, then <strong>Delete this search</strong> (mobile app) or the <strong>trash icon</strong> (web).</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
        </ol>

        <div class="helpful-widget">
            <p>Was this article helpful?</p>
            <div class="helpful-buttons">
                <button type="button">Yes</button>
                <button type="button">No</button>
            </div>
            <span>80 out of 145 found this helpful</span>
        </div>

    </div>
</div>